{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790704844,"nonce":"EIdCFEMX2sfBAuwjJa58dfGdzlM=","message":"Fixed by fd0c6f62ab1ae0d5ca65933c2acff5128a411a11.\n\nIDF placed the loop-carried `acc` phi before its unresolved initializer was lowered, so it temporarily recorded the phi as i64. Later lowering repaired the phi node, but representation-sensitive consumers had already read the stale value metadata. Lua table construction consequently emitted integer boxing for a DynamicBox pointer and retained avoidable dispatch work.\n\nThe compiler now repairs unresolved phi value metadata as soon as the initializer establishes the variable's HIR type. Lua also initializes the shared empty table array at state entry, letting shaped empty-table constructors use a direct global read.\n\nLLVM release, ZYLUA_LLVM=1, 15 interleaved direct runs on macOS:\n- compiler fix with lazy per-constructor check: 174.4 ms median\n- compiler fix plus eager shared-array initialization: 172.0 ms median (1.014x further speedup)\n- earlier affected builds clustered near 200 ms; the issue's pre-regression reference was 180 ms\n\nCorrectness:\n- compiler expression, loop-carried lowering, and block-value control-flow tests pass\n- all hand-written Lua conformance categories exercised without regressions, including errors/c_stack.lua, tables, metatables, GC stress, and warm-up variants of the directly affected groups\n- official Lua corpus was stopped after several minutes in its known long-running section; no completed group regressed","files":null}]}